<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Singara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Singara was a Roman fortress city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinjar">Sinjar</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>. It was contested between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>. The Sasanian Empire profile notes that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shapur-ii">Shapur II</a> recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nisibis">Nisibis</a>, Singara and other territory in the Treaty of Nisibis of 363 CE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/singara.jpg" alt="Singara" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Singara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
